# Repository-owned text formats are pinned to LF so cross-platform checkouts
# (Windows with core.autocrlf=true in particular) stay gofmt-clean and avoid
# go.mod / go.sum noise. See issue #67.
#
# Binary assets are intentionally left un-annotated; do not blanket-normalise
# them with this file.

# Go toolchain surfaces
*.go text eol=lf
go.mod text eol=lf
go.sum text eol=lf

# Shell installers shipped by this repo
*.sh text eol=lf

# CI and packaging manifests
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# Docs and PowerShell installer (LF lets PowerShell 5.1+ on Windows still parse it)
*.md text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# Node bin shipped via npm; keep LF so the bin shim does not embed CRLF
*.js text eol=lf

# Data files the CI gates parse. scripts/complexity-baseline.txt was the one
# extension this list missed: a Windows checkout rewrote it to CRLF, the CR
# rode along on the last field, and every arithmetic comparison in
# complexity-check.sh failed while the script still reported OK.
*.txt text eol=lf

# Extensionless files. These matched neither this list nor the CI CRLF gate,
# so all five were committed with CRLF -- including the Dockerfile, where a
# CR at the end of a RUN line becomes part of the shell command.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
